And before you ask,


00:17:02.502 --> 00:17:04.374
I handcuffed myself
for tactical reasons


00:17:04.548 --> 00:17:06.289
that I do not have time
to explain.


00:17:06.463 --> 00:17:08.334
You shouldn'’t have gone off
on your own.


00:17:08.508 --> 00:17:10.206
We'’re supposed to be a team.


00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.599
Sorry, buddy.
I'’m still working on this teamwork thing.


00:17:12.773 --> 00:17:14.297
So now what?


00:17:14.471 --> 00:17:16.647
Well, I'’m not jumping
out of any more helicopters


00:17:16.821 --> 00:17:18.823
until we get some answers
from GUN.


00:17:18.997 --> 00:17:20.564
We need somewhere to regroup.


00:17:22.087 --> 00:17:23.915
I know just the place.


00:17:24.089 --> 00:17:26.483
["Lollipop"
by TEMPURA KIDZ playing]


00:17:32.097 --> 00:17:33.664
[all clapping]


00:17:34.447 --> 00:17:36.188
<i>Hai, chiizu.</i>[yelps]


00:17:36.362 --> 00:17:37.624
It'’s an ambush!


00:17:37.798 --> 00:17:39.800
You'’ll never take us alive,
foul beasts!


00:17:39.974 --> 00:17:42.325
Calm down, Knuckles.
This is a Chao Garden.


00:17:42.499 --> 00:17:45.589
One of the top ten must-see
spots in all of Tokyo!


00:17:45.763 --> 00:17:47.678
It'’s a perfect place
for us to blend in.


00:17:47.852 --> 00:17:49.506
Are you Detective Pikachu?


00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.116
Yes, he is!


00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:54.250
[chortles] He does
look like a Pokémon.


00:17:54.424 --> 00:17:55.381
"Pika, pika!" [laughs]


00:17:55.555 --> 00:17:57.340
Commander Walters!


00:17:57.514 --> 00:17:59.298
Sonic.


00:17:59.472 --> 00:18:02.214
Thank God you'’re all okay.
I'’m sure you have questions.


00:18:02.388 --> 00:18:05.087
Just a big ticked-off
red and black one.


00:18:05.261 --> 00:18:06.653
Who was that guy?


00:18:06.827 --> 00:18:09.526
Shadow'’s story
began a lot like yours, Sonic.


00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.485
But where you found family
and friends on this planet,


00:18:12.659 --> 00:18:16.185
Shadow found only pain and loss.


00:18:16.924 --> 00:18:19.275
<i>It begins over 50 years ago,</i>


00:18:19.449 --> 00:18:22.582
<i>with a meteor crash </i>
<i>in a quiet corner of Oklahoma.</i>


00:18:22.756 --> 00:18:26.369
<i>The meteorite contained</i>
<i>a life-form.</i>


00:18:29.111 --> 00:18:30.895
<i>The ultimate life-form.</i>


00:18:32.897 --> 00:18:35.378
<i>Shadow'’s power--</i>
<i>his "chaos energy"--</i>


00:18:35.552 --> 00:18:38.555
<i>went far beyond</i>
<i>any living creature.</i>


00:18:41.166 --> 00:18:43.734
<i>The scientist</i>
<i>who discovered him</i> <i>believed this power</i>


00:18:43.908 --> 00:18:46.084
<i>would usher in a new era</i>
<i>for humanity.</i>


00:18:47.607 --> 00:18:50.741
<i>But Shadow'’s power</i>
<i>proved too dangerous.</i>


00:18:53.657 --> 00:18:55.659
<i>A terrible accident</i>
<i>destroyed the lab,</i>


00:18:55.833 --> 00:18:58.096
<i>taking human lives with it.</i>[siren wailing]


00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:02.535
<i>The project leader</i>
<i>was blamed for the incident</i> <i>and imprisoned.</i>


00:19:02.709 --> 00:19:04.363
<i>With the program canceled...</i>[yelps in pain]


00:19:04.537 --> 00:19:07.497
<i>...Shadow was a loose end </i>
<i>no one knew how to deal with.</i>


00:19:08.759 --> 00:19:10.674
<i>Too dangerous</i>
<i>to be walking free,</i>


00:19:10.848 --> 00:19:13.198
<i>too valuable to destroy.</i>


00:19:14.286 --> 00:19:16.462
<i>So I had him placed</i>
<i>into stasis...</i>


00:19:19.161 --> 00:19:21.163
<i>indefinitely.</i>


00:19:23.165 --> 00:19:26.255
Wait a second. If Shadow'’s
been on ice for 50 years,


00:19:26.429 --> 00:19:28.692
someone had to help him escape.True.


00:19:28.866 --> 00:19:30.520
But there'’s only a few people
in the world


00:19:30.694 --> 00:19:32.565
who even know
of Shadow'’s existence.


00:19:39.659 --> 00:19:42.532
[J-pop cover of
"I Want You Back" by Jackson 5 playing]


00:19:42.706 --> 00:19:44.882
[people cheering]


00:19:48.668 --> 00:19:51.105
A live show? Yeah!


00:19:54.848 --> 00:19:56.850
[drones humming]


00:20:00.419 --> 00:20:01.420
Get down!


00:20:07.426 --> 00:20:10.603
[people screaming]


00:20:11.778 --> 00:20:13.650
[groaning]


00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:17.393
Egg drones?


00:20:17.567 --> 00:20:20.265
But Robotnik
is supposed to be dead!


00:20:31.058 --> 00:20:33.322
Konnichi-what?


00:20:35.367 --> 00:20:36.586
[weapons powering up]


00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:38.501
[motorbike revving]


00:20:47.118 --> 00:20:48.772
[tires squeal]


00:20:54.256 --> 00:20:58.347
I'’m sorry, we already had
our big motorcycle chase for the evening.


00:21:03.003 --> 00:21:03.961
Commander Walters!


00:21:04.135 --> 00:21:05.397
[Knuckles grunts]


00:21:05.571 --> 00:21:07.617
[Sonic] Commander Walters,
are you okay?


00:21:08.792 --> 00:21:09.793
Sonic...


00:21:09.967 --> 00:21:11.229
[painful grunt]


00:21:12.404 --> 00:21:13.536
...take this.


00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.755
[Sonic] What is it?[Walters] A key...


00:21:16.974 --> 00:21:19.542
to the most powerful weapon
GUN has ever built.


00:21:19.716 --> 00:21:22.240
You'’re the only one I trust
to keep it safe.


00:21:22.414 --> 00:21:24.111
[exhales weakly]


00:21:24.286 --> 00:21:25.591
Commander Walters...


00:21:25.765 --> 00:21:27.289
[sirens, vehicles approaching][gasps]


00:21:31.597 --> 00:21:33.251
[indistinct shouts]


00:21:34.426 --> 00:21:35.906
Alpha team, fan out!


00:21:37.299 --> 00:21:38.691
Do we have eyes?


00:21:39.344 --> 00:21:40.345
Secure the perimeter!


00:21:43.653 --> 00:21:45.002
Medevac is en route.


00:21:45.176 --> 00:21:46.830
[indistinct radio chatter]


00:21:48.832 --> 00:21:50.312
His launch key is missing.


00:21:57.536 --> 00:21:59.756
I knew they couldn'’t be trusted.


00:22:02.019 --> 00:22:03.629
[all exclaiming]


00:22:03.803 --> 00:22:05.239
[Tails] Why are we
running from GUN?


00:22:05.414 --> 00:22:06.893
Aren'’t we on the same team?


00:22:07.067 --> 00:22:08.330
[Sonic] Until we get
more information,


00:22:08.504 --> 00:22:10.201
we'’re not trusting anyone.


00:22:10.375 --> 00:22:12.072
Follow me.Get it... off!


00:22:29.786 --> 00:22:31.788
Hold it right there,
Tokyo Drift!


00:22:31.962 --> 00:22:33.355
Who are you?


00:22:36.227 --> 00:22:38.577
[gasps] It'’s the Goat Milker!


00:22:38.751 --> 00:22:41.014
[mimicking Knuckles]
"It'’s the Goat Milker!"


00:22:41.188 --> 00:22:43.234
Relax.
I'’m not here to fight.


00:22:43.408 --> 00:22:46.455
Then why are you here?And why did you free Shadow?


00:22:46.629 --> 00:22:48.544
Are you kidding?


00:22:48.718 --> 00:22:52.330
The last thing we want
is more super-powered hedgehogs running around.


00:22:52.504 --> 00:22:54.463
The doctor had nothing
to do with it.


00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:57.988
And I can prove it.[car alarm chirps]


00:23:13.395 --> 00:23:15.005
Please,


00:23:15.179 --> 00:23:16.223
join me in the crab.


00:23:17.790 --> 00:23:20.967
[narrator] <i>And now back to... </i>
<i>"La UÚltima Pasión."</i>


00:23:21.141 --> 00:23:22.839
I have fallen in love
with another.


00:23:23.013 --> 00:23:24.797
[gasps]


00:23:24.971 --> 00:23:28.235
But who, Gabriella?
Tell me who!


00:23:30.063 --> 00:23:32.196
My twin brother, Pablo?


00:23:33.415 --> 00:23:34.851
<i>Pablo!</i>


00:23:36.766 --> 00:23:38.158
!¡Bastardo!


00:23:38.332 --> 00:23:40.726
Buenos días, !¡hermano!


00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:42.032
<i>No!</i>


00:23:42.206 --> 00:23:44.338
[cackling]


00:23:44.513 --> 00:23:46.819
Let that be a lesson
to you, Juan.


00:23:46.993 --> 00:23:48.560
[beeping]Family


00:23:48.734 --> 00:23:51.955
is a field
of emotional claymores


00:23:52.129 --> 00:23:54.348
that leave you abandoned,
betrayed


00:23:56.133 --> 00:23:59.005
and weeping
while you eat cake,


00:23:59.179 --> 00:24:01.573
which creates copious amounts
of adipose tissue,


00:24:01.747 --> 00:24:04.750
and what some calloused
individuals refer to as...


00:24:04.924 --> 00:24:07.536
[sniffs deeply]
...man boobs.


00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:08.885
Ha.


00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.063
[up-tempo Latin jazz playing]


00:24:18.242 --> 00:24:19.852
[slapping along
with the congas]


00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:23.987
[trilling loudly]


00:24:25.118 --> 00:24:26.511
[shrieking]


00:24:26.685 --> 00:24:28.731
Doctor,
we have visitors.


00:24:30.210 --> 00:24:32.212
Really?


00:24:32.386 --> 00:24:35.085
I thought I was having
an anthropomorphic nightmare.


00:24:35.259 --> 00:24:36.739
Where the only person
I could trust in the world


00:24:36.913 --> 00:24:38.436
showed up with
all my worst enemies,


00:24:38.610 --> 00:24:40.307
while I was in a bathrobe,


00:24:40.482 --> 00:24:42.745
playing congas
on my big, fat belly!


00:24:42.919 --> 00:24:44.181
Sorry, sir.


00:24:44.355 --> 00:24:46.488
I don'’t believe it.
Eggman'’s alive?


00:24:46.662 --> 00:24:49.012
And he'’s never
looked worse.


00:24:49.186 --> 00:24:51.493
[cackling] Well, maybe,


00:24:51.667 --> 00:24:55.540
this is what not giving a damn
what you think I look like looks like.


00:24:55.714 --> 00:24:58.935
Sir, right now we have
an even bigger problem.


00:24:59.109 --> 00:25:00.502
Oh, come on.


00:25:02.634 --> 00:25:04.941
There'’s an imposter out there
using your technology.


00:25:05.115 --> 00:25:08.422
Imposter.
That'’s impossi-- What?


00:25:08.597 --> 00:25:10.076
No.


00:25:10.250 --> 00:25:14.298
My sweet mechanized spawn!


00:25:14.472 --> 00:25:18.084
Whomever this party-pooping
posse is looking for


00:25:18.258 --> 00:25:20.565
has stolen my persona


00:25:20.739 --> 00:25:24.090
and the precious babies
from my egg sac.


00:25:24.787 --> 00:25:26.266
Well...


00:25:26.440 --> 00:25:30.836
I'’ll soon egg-xact
my revenge.


00:25:31.010 --> 00:25:32.664
You see what I did there?[chuckles]


00:25:32.838 --> 00:25:36.059
It'’s time for the dramatic
soap-opera twist,


00:25:36.233 --> 00:25:40.367
where this Pablo
reveals his Juan!


00:25:40.542 --> 00:25:44.415
By cross-referencing
the precise coordinates


00:25:44.589 --> 00:25:47.331
of each drone'’s
energy spikes,


00:25:48.071 --> 00:25:50.203
I can track my babies


00:25:50.377 --> 00:25:52.989
to the imposter'’s
base of operations,


00:25:53.163 --> 00:25:54.556
right about...


00:25:54.730 --> 00:25:55.557
there!


00:25:55.731 --> 00:25:57.471
Sonic, I hate to say it,


00:25:57.646 --> 00:25:59.822
but I think we'’re both
after the same person.


00:25:59.996 --> 00:26:02.433
Hold on, hold on.
You'’re not suggesting we team up


00:26:02.607 --> 00:26:04.914
with Doctor Ro-Butt-Stink,
are you?


00:26:05.088 --> 00:26:06.524
Perhaps the fox is right.


00:26:06.698 --> 00:26:09.571
It could be our only chance
to find this mysterious,


00:26:09.745 --> 00:26:11.137
more impressive hedgehog.


00:26:11.311 --> 00:26:12.486
[groans]


00:26:12.661 --> 00:26:14.706
All right, Egghead.
I hate to say it,


00:26:14.880 --> 00:26:16.447
but it looks like
we'’re partners.


00:26:17.579 --> 00:26:19.493
On one condition.


00:26:20.973 --> 00:26:23.541
Dude, you have serious issues.


00:26:23.715 --> 00:26:24.803
Ow!


00:26:27.023 --> 00:26:28.459
[gibbering spasm]


00:26:28.633 --> 00:26:29.808
Let'’s...


00:26:30.592 --> 00:26:31.723
do this!


00:26:31.897 --> 00:26:33.595
["Firestarter"
by The Prodigy playing]


00:26:40.340 --> 00:26:41.472
[pained groan]


00:26:55.007 --> 00:26:56.922
[door thuds][Robotnik grunting]


00:26:58.097 --> 00:26:59.316
Suck it in!


00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:00.665
[grunting][door rattling]


00:27:01.840 --> 00:27:03.189
Tinker-tailor?


00:27:03.363 --> 00:27:04.800
I need room.


00:27:04.974 --> 00:27:07.629
Think Elvis, circa 1976.


00:27:07.803 --> 00:27:10.066
But sir, I don'’t have
the proper materials.


00:27:11.110 --> 00:27:12.459
Found some.


00:27:14.984 --> 00:27:16.159
Resourceful.


00:27:18.596 --> 00:27:20.511
[thunder rumbling]


00:27:44.013 --> 00:27:46.015
[faint, indistinct chatter]


00:27:56.678 --> 00:27:58.767
Hey! This is a restricted area.


00:27:58.941 --> 00:28:01.204
Oh, it'’s okay.
She'’s the professor'’s granddaughter.


00:28:01.378 --> 00:28:03.510
He takes her everywhere.


00:28:03.685 --> 00:28:06.775
Welcome to the lab, Maria.
I'’m Captain Walters.


00:28:06.949 --> 00:28:08.341
Oh, do you know
where my room is?


00:28:08.515 --> 00:28:10.082
Yeah, down the hall
and to the right.


00:28:10.256 --> 00:28:11.780
Make yourself at home.


00:28:11.954 --> 00:28:13.129
But, um,


00:28:13.303 --> 00:28:15.087
let'’s lose the skates,
okay, kiddo?


00:28:15.261 --> 00:28:16.698
Okay.


00:28:21.615 --> 00:28:24.096
[machinery humming softly]


00:28:37.588 --> 00:28:39.721
[fluid bubbling faintly]


00:28:53.082 --> 00:28:54.561
[light chuckle]


00:29:02.526 --> 00:29:03.570
[chuckles]


00:29:04.920 --> 00:29:06.660
[bag rustling]


00:29:08.662 --> 00:29:09.925
[pen uncaps]


00:29:26.376 --> 00:29:27.681
[laughs]


00:29:48.224 --> 00:29:51.096
["End of the Line"
by the Traveling Wilburys playing]


00:30:16.295 --> 00:30:17.470
[delighted shriek]


00:30:17.644 --> 00:30:19.472
[squealing]


00:30:27.176 --> 00:30:28.003
[gasps]


00:30:28.177 --> 00:30:29.134
[yelling]


00:30:33.922 --> 00:30:35.097
[whooping]


00:30:36.925 --> 00:30:38.100
Look out!


00:30:39.666 --> 00:30:40.842
[crashing]


00:30:57.336 --> 00:30:58.772
[faint roaring]


00:31:16.486 --> 00:31:18.662
[song ends]


00:31:18.836 --> 00:31:20.925
[crickets chirping softly]


00:31:22.013 --> 00:31:23.188
Wow.


00:31:23.885 --> 00:31:25.321
Look at all those stars.


00:31:27.149 --> 00:31:28.977
They'’re like diamonds.


00:31:30.674 --> 00:31:32.415
My grandfather says


00:31:32.589 --> 00:31:34.243
it can take hundreds of years


00:31:34.417 --> 00:31:36.419
for the light of a star
to reach Earth.


00:31:37.159 --> 00:31:39.030
And by the time you see it,


00:31:39.204 --> 00:31:41.511
the star might not even
exist anymore.


00:31:43.034 --> 00:31:44.514
Isn'’t that crazy?


00:31:45.994 --> 00:31:47.865
A light shines,


00:31:48.039 --> 00:31:49.998
even though the star is gone.


00:31:51.564 --> 00:31:53.392
Yeah, it does.


00:31:55.220 --> 00:31:56.918
I wonder which one
you came from, Shadow.


00:31:57.092 --> 00:31:57.962
I don'’t know.


00:31:59.094 --> 00:32:01.574
I don'’t know anything
about my home.


00:32:01.748 --> 00:32:04.142
This is your home, Shadow.


00:32:04.882 --> 00:32:06.014
Earth.


00:32:12.934 --> 00:32:14.239
Maria,


00:32:14.892 --> 00:32:16.589
do you think I'’m...


00:32:17.547 --> 00:32:18.809
dangerous?


00:32:20.071 --> 00:32:21.899
What are you talking about?


00:32:22.073 --> 00:32:24.641
The way the scientists
look at me,


00:32:24.815 --> 00:32:26.512
I can tell they'’re afraid.


00:32:26.686 --> 00:32:30.255
Like I'’m the horrible thing
from that movie we watched.


00:32:31.343 --> 00:32:32.779
I don'’t know...


00:32:33.476 --> 00:32:34.956
what I am.


00:32:40.222 --> 00:32:41.788
You'’re my friend.


00:32:43.138 --> 00:32:45.792
And you can do or be
anything you want.


00:32:46.968 --> 00:32:48.578
Not because of your powers,


00:32:48.752 --> 00:32:52.190
but because of who you are...
in here.


00:32:55.019 --> 00:32:57.195
I don'’t know what I'’d do
without you.


00:33:06.988 --> 00:33:09.991
["End of the Line" resumes]


00:33:14.473 --> 00:33:16.171
[song ends abruptly]


00:33:16.345 --> 00:33:17.999
[dust crackling]


00:33:34.841 --> 00:33:36.452
[footfalls]


00:33:39.107 --> 00:33:40.804
Professor?


00:33:40.978 --> 00:33:44.025
It'’s good to see you,
Shadow.


00:33:44.199 --> 00:33:46.288
I knew you'’d come home.


00:33:46.462 --> 00:33:49.030
I can'’t get her out of my head.


00:33:49.204 --> 00:33:50.727
The pain...


00:33:50.901 --> 00:33:52.250
It'’s too much.


00:33:52.424 --> 00:33:55.906
And that is why
we have to punish them.


00:34:00.432 --> 00:34:02.043
Okay, I don'’t like you
and you don'’t like me.


00:34:02.217 --> 00:34:04.045
Let'’s get this
over with quickly.


00:34:04.219 --> 00:34:06.047
Out of my way, dorkupine.


00:34:06.221 --> 00:34:08.310
"Dorkupine"?
Really clever.


00:34:12.749 --> 00:34:14.620
[hollow tapping]


00:34:14.794 --> 00:34:16.883
This door is six-inch-thick
solid steel


00:34:17.058 --> 00:34:18.842
on a pressurized latch.


00:34:19.016 --> 00:34:21.192
I'’ll need a moment to calculate
the molecular density


00:34:21.366 --> 00:34:22.976
and invert
the venting mechanics.


00:34:23.151 --> 00:34:24.587
[thunderous crash]


00:34:26.632 --> 00:34:27.894
[Knuckles] I unlocked it.


00:34:28.069 --> 00:34:31.072
[Robotnik] Subtle as always,
fist-for-brains.


00:34:32.334 --> 00:34:34.075
Easy, Shadow.


00:34:34.249 --> 00:34:36.729
Those are the guests
I'’ve been expecting.


00:34:36.903 --> 00:34:39.558
Let'’s give them
a warm welcome.


00:34:43.388 --> 00:34:44.737
[Stone] Whoa.


00:34:44.911 --> 00:34:46.174
What is this place?


00:34:46.348 --> 00:34:48.306
[Sonic] It looks like
a military base,


00:34:48.480 --> 00:34:50.308
but nobody'’s been here
for years.


00:34:50.482 --> 00:34:51.875
I wonder if it'’s haunted.


00:34:52.049 --> 00:34:54.965
Haunted? Nobody said anything
about being haunted.


00:34:55.139 --> 00:34:58.099
What'’s the matter?
You afraid of g-g-g-ghosts?


00:34:58.273 --> 00:35:00.362
Nothing scares
an Echidna warrior.


00:35:00.536 --> 00:35:02.929
Uh, yeah. Do you remember
what happened last movie night?


00:35:03.104 --> 00:35:04.670
[screaming in terror]


00:35:04.844 --> 00:35:06.150
[piercing scream][all yelling]


00:35:06.324 --> 00:35:07.760
Let go, let go, let go!


00:35:07.934 --> 00:35:10.633
There is no such thing
as a friendly ghost.


00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:13.723
[Sonic]
So which way do we go?


00:35:13.897 --> 00:35:17.596
I know! We should split up.


00:35:17.770 --> 00:35:20.991
Everyone with hideous,
brightly-colored fur take the left and the middle.


00:35:21.165 --> 00:35:22.775
Stone and I will go right.


00:35:22.949 --> 00:35:24.690
No, no, no, no, no. I'’m not
letting you out of my sight.


00:35:24.864 --> 00:35:26.649
Tails, you and Stone go left.


00:35:26.823 --> 00:35:29.913
Knuckles, you take the middle.
Eggman, you and me go right.


00:35:30.087 --> 00:35:32.002
By all means.


00:35:32.176 --> 00:35:33.656
We could use some
time together.


00:35:33.830 --> 00:35:35.440
To work on
your trust issues.


00:35:35.614 --> 00:35:38.443
You know what? You'’re right.
I should be more trusting.


00:35:38.617 --> 00:35:41.403
I mean, you'’ve only tried
to kill me twice!


00:35:43.448 --> 00:35:45.668
Just a dark, creepy hallway.


00:35:45.842 --> 00:35:47.539
Nothing to be afraid of.


00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.977
You hear that, ghost?


00:35:51.152 --> 00:35:52.675
You don'’t frighten me!


00:35:52.849 --> 00:35:54.416
[steam hissing][yells]


00:35:57.158 --> 00:35:59.551
Get... a... grip.


00:36:00.465 --> 00:36:02.206
Boo.[screams]


00:36:04.904 --> 00:36:07.603
I'’m just gonna
come right out and say this:


00:36:07.777 --> 00:36:10.562
You'’re adorable.[chuckles]
Oh, um, thanks.


00:36:10.736 --> 00:36:14.175
So, what'’s it like
being Sonic'’s assistant?


00:36:14.349 --> 00:36:17.656
You have a daily routine?
Paid time off? Benefits?


00:36:17.830 --> 00:36:21.007
Oh, I'’m not Sonic'’s assistant.
We'’re teammates.


00:36:21.182 --> 00:36:23.184
He'’s the leader,
Knuckles is the muscle,


00:36:23.358 --> 00:36:24.924
and I'’m the gadget guy.


00:36:25.098 --> 00:36:26.448
We all have a role to play.


00:36:26.622 --> 00:36:28.363
That'’s what makes the team
so special!


00:36:28.537 --> 00:36:30.278
That and the fact
we'’re best friends.


00:36:31.017 --> 00:36:32.323
You are?


00:36:32.497 --> 00:36:34.325
Well, yeah.
Just like you and Eggman, right?


00:36:36.153 --> 00:36:38.199
Uh... Yeah, eh...


00:36:38.373 --> 00:36:40.375
Of course! Yes.


00:36:40.549 --> 00:36:43.421
Me and the doctor,
best of friends.


00:36:44.901 --> 00:36:46.468
That'’s definitely
what we are.


00:36:46.642 --> 00:36:48.774
[metallic clattering]


00:36:48.948 --> 00:36:50.733
[squeaking]


00:36:51.690 --> 00:36:52.735
Hmm.


00:36:57.740 --> 00:36:59.481
[both screaming]


00:37:11.841 --> 00:37:15.410
Whoa. Look at all this stuff.


00:37:15.584 --> 00:37:18.717
This was more than
just a military base or a lab.


00:37:19.283 --> 00:37:20.719
It was a home.


00:37:20.893 --> 00:37:22.460
People lived here.


00:37:23.069 --> 00:37:24.549
He had a family.


00:37:25.289 --> 00:37:27.117
Is that what I smell?


00:37:27.291 --> 00:37:30.381
The stench
of domestic harmony?


00:37:30.555 --> 00:37:34.080
You ever wonder what
your life would have been like if you had a family?


00:37:34.255 --> 00:37:35.691
Hmm... No!


00:37:35.865 --> 00:37:37.867
Maybe you wouldn'’t have gone
full supervillain.


00:37:38.041 --> 00:37:40.870
I have no parents,
no aunts, no uncles.


00:37:41.044 --> 00:37:43.568
And something about my attitude
renders me...


00:37:44.526 --> 00:37:48.660
undesirable
to all possible genders.


00:37:50.532 --> 00:37:52.708
My future is a cul-de-sac!


00:37:53.709 --> 00:37:55.711
The Robotnik name ends...


00:37:57.365 --> 00:37:59.018
<i>avec moi.</i>


00:37:59.192 --> 00:38:01.238
Yes, I know French.


00:38:02.283 --> 00:38:03.762
[shuddering spasm]


00:38:05.764 --> 00:38:06.852
Whoa.


00:38:07.026 --> 00:38:10.029
Is this where you grew up,
Shadow?


00:38:10.203 --> 00:38:11.988
No wonder you'’re so mad.


00:38:12.162 --> 00:38:15.034
This place could really use
a beanbag chair


00:38:15.208 --> 00:38:16.514
and some comic books.


00:38:18.037 --> 00:38:19.256
What happened here?


00:38:19.952 --> 00:38:21.127
[hard grunt]


00:38:21.302 --> 00:38:23.434
I'’m tired
of giving you warnings!


00:38:24.305 --> 00:38:26.307
[grunts, yells]


00:38:27.308 --> 00:38:28.700
Where'’d you go, hedgehog?


00:38:28.874 --> 00:38:30.746
I wasn'’t finished
trauma dumping.


00:38:32.574 --> 00:38:35.359
My darlings!


00:38:35.533 --> 00:38:37.056
[inhales, giggles]


00:38:37.230 --> 00:38:39.668
My eggy weggies!


00:38:40.799 --> 00:38:43.846
[professor] ♪ <i>Memories</i>♪


00:38:44.020 --> 00:38:47.371
♪ <i>Light the corners</i>♪


00:38:47.545 --> 00:38:51.201
♪ <i>Of my mind</i>♪


00:38:51.375 --> 00:38:54.509
♪ <i>Misty watercolor</i>♪


00:38:54.683 --> 00:39:00.297
♪ <i>Memories</i>♪


00:39:00.471 --> 00:39:03.344
♪ <i>Of the way</i>♪


00:39:03.518 --> 00:39:08.784
♪ <i>We weren'’t</i>♪


00:39:09.741 --> 00:39:10.742
I...


00:39:12.483 --> 00:39:14.224
don'’t believe it.Don'’t you?


00:39:14.398 --> 00:39:15.660
It'’s impossible.Is it?


00:39:15.834 --> 00:39:16.748
It couldn'’t be.Couldn'’t it?


00:39:16.922 --> 00:39:17.706
I'’m--Are you?


00:39:17.880 --> 00:39:19.055
Imposter!


00:39:19.229 --> 00:39:21.492
You stole my babies!


00:39:21.666 --> 00:39:24.843
But they know
who their real daddy is...


00:39:25.017 --> 00:39:26.105
drone-napper!


00:39:26.279 --> 00:39:27.803
[chortling]


00:39:27.977 --> 00:39:31.067
Magnificent creations,
my boy.


00:39:31.241 --> 00:39:33.809
I borrowed them
to lure you here


00:39:33.983 --> 00:39:35.985
and reunite our family.


00:39:37.726 --> 00:39:39.380
You see, Ivo...


00:39:41.512 --> 00:39:44.515
I'’m your grandfather:


00:39:44.689 --> 00:39:47.126
Gerald Robotnik.


00:39:51.174 --> 00:39:53.872
My... grandfather?


00:39:55.613 --> 00:39:58.486
But how? And why?


00:39:59.269 --> 00:40:01.314
And who did what with whom?


00:40:01.489 --> 00:40:06.407
You hail from an ancestry
of excellence...


00:40:06.581 --> 00:40:09.148
tied directly <i>à moi.</i>


00:40:09.322 --> 00:40:12.238
Yes, I know French.


00:40:14.763 --> 00:40:16.286
You do look like me.


00:40:17.243 --> 00:40:19.202
But fatter. And older.


00:40:20.072 --> 00:40:22.031
And there'’s that funny smell.


00:40:23.728 --> 00:40:26.557
But the resemblance
is uncanny.


00:40:27.428 --> 00:40:29.038
It'’s as if...


00:40:29.212 --> 00:40:31.301
[both]
...we'’re two characters in a movie


00:40:31.475 --> 00:40:34.043
